# Explain

Every panel answers "what is this?" without leaving the screen. Press ? on
any panel for its card. Card text lives in glossary.md, so it is written once
and reviewed like any other doc.

## ◆ExplainCard

@modal
┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ ? Gameplan                                   esc close │
├────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                                                        │
│ The record of what's built, in progress, and next.     │
│ Work is grouped into phases; one phase is active and   │
│ is broken into tasks. When a task ships, its           │
│ resolution is written here so the next session (or     │
│ the next person) doesn't have to dig through git.      │
│                                                        │
│ Lives in .daedalus/roadmap/gameplan.json (committed).  │
│ CLI: daedalus gameplan show                            │
│                                                        │
├────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ g glossary · esc close                                 │
└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
note: three parts, always: what it is, where it lives, the CLI that shows it.
The last line teaches the CLI, so the TUI is a way in, not a dead end.

## ◆Welcome

@first-run
┌────────────────────────────────┐
│ Welcome to Daedalus            │
├────────────────────────────────┤
│                                │
│ Nothing here yet. Daedalus     │
│ fills these panels as you      │
│ work:                          │
│                                │
│ · a gameplan (what's next)     │
│ · edicts (your decisions)      │
│ · session notes (what          │
│   happened)                    │
│                                │
│ ? what is all this             │
│ c ask Claude to start a plan   │
└────────────────────────────────┘
note: an empty state teaches; it never just says "no data".
